 "result_text": "`$ext` in an MQTT publish `json` block should now be evaluated, but I haven't run anything, so the fix is untested.\n\nYour request was configured correctly. The bug was ordering. `get_publish_args` in `tavern/_plugins/mqtt/request.py` turned `json` into a string with `json.dumps` before `update_from_ext(publish_args, [\"json\"])` ran. By then there was no `json` key left, and the `$ext` was buried inside the string.\n\nI moved the `update_from_ext(fspec, [\"json\"])` call into `get_publish_args`, so it runs before the dump. It removes the `$ext` key and merges the function's return value into the `json` dict. The old call in `MQTTRequest.__init__` is gone.\n\nYour suggestion to use `[\"payload\"]` wouldn't have worked, since `payload` is the already-serialized string.\n\nI didn't touch tests, and nothing is committed.",
